WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:01.580
A number machine.

2
00:00:01.630 --> 00:00:03.410
A mystery number goes in.

3
00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:06.330
The machine doubles it, then adds three.

4
00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:08.070
Out comes thirteen.

5
00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:09.610
So what went in?

6
00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:11.600
Someone tries to work backwards.

7
00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:14.080
Halve thirteen: six point five.

8
00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:16.640
Take away three: three point five.

9
00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:17.450
Check it.

10
00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:20.430
Three point five, doubled, plus three.

11
00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:22.530
That doesn't come back to thirteen.

12
00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:24.410
The undoing went wrong.

13
00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:28.060
Why should you subtract
three first, not halve first?

14
00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:31.750
In this mission, you'll treat
a function as a chain of steps.

15
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.210
A composite function applies one function,

16
00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:36.200
then another to the result.

17
00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:39.030
You'll meet the inverse
function, f inverse,

18
00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:42.140
which undoes f, and learn how to find it.

19
00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:45.950
Your mission: explain why
you subtract three first.
